# xBLiMPs runs local-first — no backend is required to develop or use the app.
# Persistence is an append-only op-log in localStorage (see src/lib/store.ts).
#
# To make persistence networked + collaborative, implement the flush target in
# src/lib/sync.ts against Google Sheets `batchUpdate` or Supabase `upsert`, keyed
# on (entity, row_uid, op_id). Then copy this file to `.env` and fill in:

# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
